WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.104 align:start size:97% position:3%
- One of the scariest parts
that sort of came out of Covid

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:08.208
was that if you were accused
of spreading misinformation,

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:10.610
and misinformation
was narrowly defined

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.045
as Covid misinformation,

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.814 align:start position:0%
but now it's defined more
broadly into any misinformation.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.984
And so, reproductive
health in the wake

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.652
of Roe v. Wade falling,

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.554 align:start size:84% position:16%
if you are spreading
misinformation

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.824
about reproductive health,
your license is at risk.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.359 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so I wrote a piece
for "The Spectator"

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.628
about the fall of Roe v.
Wade and all these things,

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:31.398
and no one would talk to me on
the record because they said,

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.866
"I can lose my license."

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.068
And who defines misinformation

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.236
and who makes these decisions?

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.570
All of it is secret.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.639
And so I can just get a
letter one day that says

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:41.041
I've had my license revoked.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:81% position:19%
And so, all of
this is permeating

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:48.148 align:start size:88% position:13%
through licensing for
psychiatry, for medical.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:51.785
To get into med school you
have to answer questions,

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.386
you know, it's a litmus test.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:57.090
How will you implement DEI
in your professional life

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a medical
professional of any kind?

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:04.664
(gentle music)

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.568
- I'm Dave Rubin,

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.870 align:start size:97% position:3%
and joining me today are
the authors of the new book,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:14.407 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Stolen Youth: How Radicals
Are Erasing Innocence

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.743 align:start size:81% position:19%
and Indoctrinating
A Generation",

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.978 align:start size:84% position:16%
Karol Markowicz
and Bethany Mandel.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.381
Karol, Bethany, welcome
to "The Rubin Report".

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.615
- Thank you.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.883
- Karol, this must
be freaking you out

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.351
because we usually
do this over Skype

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.320
or in person when we're drunk.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.056 align:start size:88% position:13%
But here we are sober
in the middle of the day

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.524
talking about stuff.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.560 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Hard to not fix my hair
and look at myself, you know.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.794
(Dave laughing)

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:35.929 align:start size:84% position:16%
- And Bethany, we've
never met before.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.197
- No, no.

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:39.432
- But you're in the
mix of these mothers

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.634
who are fighting this lunacy.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.670
- Yeah, I just tag along
with Karol, basically.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.706
- How did you guys decide
to write a book together?

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.007
- I'll go to the
new person first.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.309
I'm gonna have to blend this,

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.777
I don't wanna cause a
cat fight here, right?

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.278 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Obviously, obviously, yeah.
(Bethany laughing)

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.080 align:start position:0%
- So, Karol and I have been
friends for a really long time.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.583
It's hard to do,
but we're friends.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.918
And we have very
similar worldviews,

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.421
and she writes the columns
that I always meant to write

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.089
but didn't get around
to emailing the editor,

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.290
and then I'd read
it and I'm like,

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.159 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Dang, she did that
better than I would've."

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, we'd been talking
about it for years.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:12.899 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we had another iteration
of the book proposal,

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.001
"Get Your Village
Off My Children",

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.003
and then Covid hit.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.539 align:start size:84% position:16%
Everything froze
and we sort of said,

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:22.075
"Let's see where
the dust settles."

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.277 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then the dust
settled and we realized,

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wow, 'Get Your Village
Off My Children' is legit.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.182
We really need to get them
away from our children."

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:30.383
And so we said,

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:35.288 align:start size:97% position:3%
"There is this woke stuff
happening younger and younger,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.091 align:start size:81% position:19%
but do we have
enough for a book?

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.225
Is there enough material here?"

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.494
And so we started a Google Doc,

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:44.063
and we just started
dumping stuff in.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.933 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we realized after a
week, we have too much stuff.

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.501
The problem isn't,
is there a book?

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.770
It's like, how can we only
write one book about this,

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.138
and how do we narrow this down?

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.874
And so, we just
started plugging.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.678
I don't know how
much you wanna say,

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
but do you wanna take over
this part of the story?

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.215 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, sure.
- Well, let me maybe do

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.583
a little bio part first

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.118 align:start size:97% position:3%
before we get fully to that
- Yeah, sorry.

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:06.653
- just so that people have
a frame of reference here.

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.588
Why don't you both say how
many kids you have, ages,

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:11.591
things like that, that kind of
frame this in a personal way.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.927
- So, Bethany Mandel,

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:18.665 align:start size:97% position:3%
I am a columnist for "Deseret
News" and "Fox News".

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.401
I write things, places.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:22.235
- You're on Twitter?

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.003
- Yeah, I do the tweets.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.206
And I'm an editor of a
children's book series

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.074
that is super patriotic
and wonderful called,

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.509
"Heroes Of Liberty".

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:32.412
And I have six kids,
aged nine and under.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:33.680 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Six, nine and under?
- Six, yeah.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.548
- I just met the two-month-old.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:36.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, he's really cute.
- My God,

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:37.217
you're really going for it.

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.051
- Yeah.
- Karol.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.552
- I'm Karol Markowicz.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.554
I'm a columnist at the "New
York Post" and "Fox News",

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.089
and I have only three kids,

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:46.025
which seems like a lot
until you meet Bethany.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.728 align:start size:97% position:3%
- As someone with two,
three does seem like a lot.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:49.963
- You gotta catch up, really.

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:51.598
- So, you guys, you get
this Google Doc going

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:52.865
and your dumping stuff in there.

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.667
Trust me, I wish I could
wake up on any given day

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.603 align:start size:84% position:16%
and have no woke
thing to go crazy over

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:57.770
so I can see how
this thing would be

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.172
expanding and expanding.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:01.441
And then, how did you
decide to frame it

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.343
sort of purely around education?

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:05.078 align:start size:97% position:3%
And was that just from being
moms and you were like,

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:07.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This is clearly the
thing that matters most."?

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:09.582
- So we have two different
paths that we have taken.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.584
I have kids in public
and private schools.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.686
I have two sons in public
and a daughter in private,

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.121
and Bethany homeschools.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:18.458 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so what we were
seeing was during Covid

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.594 align:start size:81% position:19%
kids were just
the last priority.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.496
They just completely
weren't considered.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.398
They would post re-opening plans

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:27.400
and not even put
children in them.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.135
They had to live
under restrictions

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.637
far longer than anybody else.

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:34.140 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we saw that it was really
getting to be a problem

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:37.577 align:start size:97% position:3%
where kids were just not
considered in society at all.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.979
And so our book focuses on that,

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:43.082 align:start size:88% position:13%
but also on how schools
are targeting them

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:48.087
and publishing companies and
libraries and doctor's offices,

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:51.724
all of it targeting for
woke indoctrination.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.960
- Are you shocked at
the amount of parents

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:58.231 align:start position:0%
that just go along with whatever
crazy thing happens next?

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:01.000
I mean, I can tell you as
a father of a six-month-old

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.003 align:start size:88% position:13%
and a four-month-old,
the idea that, you know,

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:08.341
is it the CDC or the NIH now,
they wanna put in the schedule

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.777
the Covid vaccination
for six-month-olds.

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:13.246
There's no chance in hell!

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.981
Literally, over my dead body.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:18.685
But they do things and then
people just go along with it.

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:20.153
Was that shocking to see,

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.789 align:start size:84% position:16%
or is that just
kind of Parent 101?

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:26.426
- No, it's actually the
opposite of Parent 101.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:27.727
- Not what Parent 101 should be.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:30.029
I mean, the way it
functions, maybe.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:32.398
- What you're supposed to do
is lay your life on the line

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.934
and do anything possible
to save your children,

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.704
to help your children in
any way, shape, or form.

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:39.739 align:start size:84% position:16%
And what we saw over
Covid, I'm sorry,

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:41.507
but was a lot of parents saying,

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.209 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Well, I don't wanna
be the loudmouth.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.477
I don't wanna be
the troublemaker."

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:46.412
And so they went along with it.

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.348
One of the craziest things
that happened over Covid,

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:49.782
and our book isn't
just about Covid,

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.517
there's so, so much more to it.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:54.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
But, this sort of
drove it home for me.

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:57.156
Last summer, summer of '22.

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.392 align:start size:84% position:16%
Right, that was '22?
- Mm hm, yes.

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:00.626
- Yeah.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:01.294
- (laughs)It's going
faster and faster.

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:02.562
- It really is.

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:05.264
I sent my kids to a
violin summer camp.

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:09.268
Signed them up, first day of
summer camp I dropped them off

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.270
and every single kid
was wearing a mask.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.539
And I thought, "Gosh,
that's awfully weird."

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.375
Didn't think anything of it.

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:20.913
I got a call from the camp,
"We're requiring masks."

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.383
And I was completely shocked.

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:25.051 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's no mask
mandate in the county,

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:27.253
no mask mandate in the
park that they're in.

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:31.491
We're past masks, why
are you requiring masks

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:34.460
only for the summer
camp at this park?

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.729
And they said, "Well, it's
to protect the children."

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:41.134
As if my biggest imperative
isn't to protect my children.

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:44.871
And I came in guns
blazing, furious.

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:47.840
And I pulled my kids out and
they said, "Sorry, no refund."

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.076 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I said, "Oh, you do not
know who you're dealing with."

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:50.910
(all laughing)
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.445
- Do you?

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.480
And I said, "I want the name
of your board of directors,

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.115
I want all of their
contact information,

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:57.617
and let's have a conversation

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:59.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
about how this bait and
switch situation happened,

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:01.587
and about how you
have no concern

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:04.724
about the future of children
and the wellbeing of children."

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:08.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why was I the only parent
that was horrified?

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:10.296
Every other parent
dropped their kid off

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:14.901
dutifully in a mask for a music
camp in the middle of summer

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:16.169
in a literal swamp.

00:07:16.169 --> 00:07:19.172
We call DC the swamp for
a reason, it is a swamp.

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:22.108
And every single parent just
said, "You know, this is-"

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:24.243
And I had a lot of
work to do that week.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:27.013
I had piled all the rest
of my work that summer,

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:29.582
including for this
book, into that week.

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:31.451 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I pulled my
kids out and I said,

00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:33.886 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Okay, looks like I'm
not sleeping this week."

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:36.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I did mommy camp
with them the whole week,

00:07:36.589 --> 00:07:40.593 align:start size:84% position:16%
and from 7:00 PM until
2:00 AM I worked.

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:42.829 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I don't understand
why more parents

00:07:42.829 --> 00:07:44.730
didn't take that perspective.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.766
- So Karol, you were,
I know this factually,

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:48.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were dealing with
this nonsense in Brooklyn

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:51.337 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the crazy things they were
putting your kids through.

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:53.973
What was the snap point for you?

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:55.208
- Well, the snap point was

00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:56.509
I saw that nothing
was getting better.

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:59.979
But just for a slight
defense of parents,

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:03.082
I would say that Covid
ran in to cancel culture

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:05.952
in such a way that
parents were afraid

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:08.955 align:start size:97% position:3%
of having their lives
destroyed if they spoke out

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:10.122
and if they spoke up.

00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:11.858 align:start size:84% position:16%
And while that doesn't
excuse anybody,

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:13.926 align:start size:97% position:3%
they should still be pulling
their kids out of camps

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:15.862
and doing stuff like that.

00:08:15.862 --> 00:08:20.433 align:start position:0%
It does explain why parents
didn't fight harder at the time.

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:22.468
People did get fired for saying,

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:23.936 align:start size:97% position:3%
"This school should open."
- And we all pick our battles.

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.037
We all pick our battles.

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:26.572
Did I mask my kids at moments

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.140
that I did not feel
comfortable with?

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.076
Absolutely, I did.

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:33.012 align:start size:84% position:16%
But, that summer of
2022 really killed me.

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:34.514
- Right.

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:36.215
A little bit past the point
where any of this made sense.

00:08:36.215 --> 00:08:38.217
And I think many people would
argue it never made sense,

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:39.819
and that's a whole other thing.

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:42.588 align:start size:84% position:16%
So when you would
talk to other parents,

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:44.757
when you do this
at the violin camp

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:48.528 align:start size:97% position:3%
or now you're talking to
parents at your kids' schools,

00:08:48.528 --> 00:08:50.329
was it really just fear,

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:52.899 align:start size:97% position:3%
or is it just that people
actually had no freaking clue?

00:08:52.899 --> 00:08:54.834
Like, in some ways
they're not adults.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:56.068
Something like that.

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:58.538 align:start size:84% position:16%
We have a Gen X
generation of people

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:00.239
that never fully became adults.

00:09:00.239 --> 00:09:01.674
- It was a combination.

00:09:01.674 --> 00:09:04.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
In Brooklyn. I had people
who were just like,

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:05.244
"Well, the CDC says.

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:07.413 align:start size:84% position:16%
And if the CDC
says, then I do it.

00:09:07.413 --> 00:09:08.881 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the doctors say."
(Dave laughing)

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:11.017
And I would be like, "No, the
doctors don't really say."

