And both of them told me
there's a sex scene in it

00:36:09.901 --> 00:36:11.502
between two girls
at a sleepover.

00:36:11.502 --> 00:36:14.539 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I was like, "I
don't want my daughter

00:36:14.539 --> 00:36:17.542 align:start size:97% position:3%
thinking she can have a sexual
encounter at a sleepover."

00:36:17.542 --> 00:36:20.678
That seems like a road
that I don't wanna open.

00:36:22.613 --> 00:36:25.249
The second time the mother
described it in more detail,

00:36:25.249 --> 00:36:28.419
I thought, "Girl, soccer
player, graphic novel.

00:36:28.419 --> 00:36:30.254
What did we pick up at
the library last week?

00:36:30.254 --> 00:36:31.989
I feel like that
sounds familiar."

00:36:31.989 --> 00:36:35.092 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I hung up the phone, got
my iPhone flashlight out,

00:36:35.092 --> 00:36:37.595 align:start size:97% position:3%
opened my trunk, went into the
bag with the library books,

00:36:37.595 --> 00:36:39.063
and there it was.

00:36:39.063 --> 00:36:40.565 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I said, "Oh, well I
could quote this extensively

00:36:40.565 --> 00:36:42.900
'cause my daughter picked it
out at the library this week."

00:36:42.900 --> 00:36:44.869 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I hadn't brought
the book in, and I said,

00:36:44.869 --> 00:36:46.604
"That's it for us
at the library.

00:36:46.604 --> 00:36:48.039
I'm done."

00:36:48.039 --> 00:36:49.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was ironic because
I spent all of Covid

00:36:49.574 --> 00:36:51.943 align:start size:84% position:16%
fighting with my local
library to reopen,

00:36:51.943 --> 00:36:53.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't remember the last
time I've been there.

00:36:53.644 --> 00:36:57.415
- Isn't it weird how
it ultimately became
a war on normalcy?

00:36:57.415 --> 00:36:59.617
Remember when Megyn
Kelly finally had her

00:36:59.617 --> 00:37:01.118
final straw with all this

00:37:01.118 --> 00:37:03.754
after they were doing all of
this stuff at her kid's school

00:37:03.754 --> 00:37:05.223
on the upper West side.

00:37:05.223 --> 00:37:07.191 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then she took a picture,
I think, of a bookstore

00:37:07.191 --> 00:37:08.659
that I used to live
a block away from

00:37:08.659 --> 00:37:11.229
on Amsterdam and 83rd,

00:37:11.229 --> 00:37:14.332
it was literally like woke
superheroes or something

00:37:14.332 --> 00:37:15.866
in the bookstore window.

00:37:15.866 --> 00:37:18.236 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then she was like, "Okay,
I gotta leave this city."

00:37:18.236 --> 00:37:20.238
Like, that they just everywhere.

00:37:20.238 --> 00:37:21.172
- That's really what it was.

00:37:21.172 --> 00:37:23.140
It was the war on normalcy,

00:37:23.140 --> 00:37:24.642
that's what drove
us out of New York.

00:37:24.642 --> 00:37:27.878 align:start position:0%
It was that we didn't see
normalcy returning for a while,

00:37:27.878 --> 00:37:29.413
and childhoods very short.

00:37:29.413 --> 00:37:32.283
So we didn't want our kids
to be growing up in that.

00:37:32.283 --> 00:37:34.585 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I think that's
the real thing

00:37:34.585 --> 00:37:37.555 align:start position:0%
parents need to give their kids,
that stability and normalcy

00:37:37.555 --> 00:37:39.557
so that they grow up
and they're resilient.

00:37:39.557 --> 00:37:42.593 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's the goal,
raising resilient children.

00:37:42.593 --> 00:37:44.128
- Yeah.

00:37:44.128 --> 00:37:45.329
- Well, Bethany, you walked
in here with a two-month-old

00:37:45.329 --> 00:37:46.831
who then you handed
to my assistant.

00:37:46.831 --> 00:37:48.699
We haven't heard anything
in the last 40 minutes,

00:37:48.699 --> 00:37:50.568
so I feel like it's probably

00:37:50.568 --> 00:37:52.069
going okay out there.
- Fingers crossed.

00:37:52.069 --> 00:37:54.472 align:start size:97% position:3%
Or she's taken him, in which
case, I have five spares.

00:37:54.472 --> 00:37:57.174
So, good luck to her.

00:37:57.174 --> 00:37:59.110
- Any final thoughts, ladies?

00:37:59.110 --> 00:38:00.645 align:start size:84% position:16%
We will link to
the book down below

00:38:00.645 --> 00:38:01.879 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we'll do our best
to get you on the

00:38:01.879 --> 00:38:03.381
"New York Times"
Bestseller List.

00:38:03.381 --> 00:38:04.782
But of course, you know,
that's completely made up

00:38:04.782 --> 00:38:07.285
because they're woke and
they are not big fans.

00:38:07.285 --> 00:38:08.119 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Greta Thunbergs at the top.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:38:08.953 --> 00:38:10.221
- Well, that's the thing

00:38:10.221 --> 00:38:11.856
that really people
should understand

00:38:11.856 --> 00:38:13.791 align:start size:84% position:16%
is that this has
permeated everything.

00:38:13.791 --> 00:38:18.796
You think that something is
normal or fair or standard,

00:38:19.397 --> 00:38:20.598
and it's not.

00:38:20.598 --> 00:38:21.532 align:start size:84% position:16%
And "New York Times"
Bestseller List

00:38:21.532 --> 00:38:22.767
is a great example of that where

00:38:22.767 --> 00:38:24.669
it doesn't matter how
many books you sell,

00:38:24.669 --> 00:38:26.804
the Greta Thunberg example,

00:38:26.804 --> 00:38:29.707 align:start size:97% position:3%
she was on the bestseller list
last week with 4,000 books.

00:38:29.707 --> 00:38:33.077 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm sure that you sold more.
- I sold way more.

00:38:33.077 --> 00:38:34.512 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Way more, and you were not.
- I should have been

00:38:34.512 --> 00:38:36.314 align:start size:97% position:3%
number two, possibly number
one for my last book.

00:38:36.314 --> 00:38:37.715
They didn't even put me on it.

00:38:37.715 --> 00:38:38.983 align:start size:84% position:16%
And on my first book
they put me at 11

00:38:38.983 --> 00:38:40.418
when I should have been four.

00:38:40.418 --> 00:38:41.686 align:start size:84% position:16%
- That's really
what we're fighting.

00:38:41.686 --> 00:38:43.554
- And I sold 10 times
more than number four.

00:38:43.554 --> 00:38:44.655 align:start size:84% position:16%
- That's what we're
fighting here.

00:38:44.655 --> 00:38:47.425
It's that this abnormal behavior

00:38:47.425 --> 00:38:50.294
and this push of
just one viewpoint

00:38:50.294 --> 00:38:52.263
is permeating everything,

00:38:52.263 --> 00:38:54.298
and you have to keep
your kids from it.

00:38:54.298 --> 00:38:55.833
- Yeah.

00:38:55.833 --> 00:38:58.569
I mean, the final thought for
me is the resilience chapter.

00:38:58.569 --> 00:39:00.204 align:start size:84% position:16%
That was the last
chapter that I wrote

00:39:00.204 --> 00:39:03.541 align:start size:97% position:3%
and told a very personal
story of my mom passing away

00:39:03.541 --> 00:39:06.243 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the circumstances of
that when I was 16 years old.

00:39:06.243 --> 00:39:09.547
I was the one that pulled
the plug, spoiler alert,

00:39:09.547 --> 00:39:12.183
and I was raised resilient.

00:39:12.183 --> 00:39:15.586
And I went to a therapist
who gave me some tough love

00:39:15.586 --> 00:39:17.988 align:start size:88% position:13%
and said, "Do not define
yourself as a victim.

00:39:19.523 --> 00:39:20.758
If it's not who you want to be,

00:39:20.758 --> 00:39:22.593
do not define yourself as such."

00:39:22.593 --> 00:39:26.297
What are the chances of a
16 year old Bethany today

00:39:26.297 --> 00:39:28.466
having a therapist who
would say that to her?

00:39:28.466 --> 00:39:30.568
Now victimhood is the goal.

00:39:30.568 --> 00:39:32.870
It's not something
that you wanna avoid.

00:39:32.870 --> 00:39:35.673 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it's creating a
generation of children

00:39:35.673 --> 00:39:38.542 align:start position:0%
who are not just not resilient,
but who are basket cases.

00:39:38.542 --> 00:39:40.578 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's the goal.
- Alright.

00:39:40.578 --> 00:39:43.714 align:start size:88% position:13%
Well to end this, we
can reveal our plan now.

00:39:43.714 --> 00:39:45.316
You guys went through
this whole process

00:39:45.316 --> 00:39:47.051
of writing this whole
book, coming here,

00:39:47.051 --> 00:39:49.754
et cetera, et cetera,
but it was really,

00:39:49.754 --> 00:39:51.122
should we hold her
hand while we say it?

00:39:51.122 --> 00:39:52.056
- Yeah, you're gonna
live in Florida now.

00:39:52.056 --> 00:39:53.290
- It was to move you to Florida.

00:39:53.290 --> 00:39:54.625
- With my one suitcase

00:39:54.625 --> 00:39:56.127 align:start size:97% position:3%
and my two-month-old. (laughs)
- You're staying.

00:39:56.127 --> 00:39:58.829 align:start size:97% position:3%
There is no flight back, and
your child has been taken

00:39:58.829 --> 00:40:00.231
